  "features": [
    "Node resource timing entries carry live timing references, body/cache/status/delivery metadata and JSON getters with class/receiver validation.",
    "Node timeline queries, clearing, buffered resource observation, overflow recovery and event listener/property forwarding are connected to the shared registry.",
    "Three WebCore resource/metrics implementations compile from Home, replacing external objects; eight selected implementation/header files match the pin with byte-identical ABI/cache checks."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Global WebCore markResourceTiming still returns undefined; native overflow processing and automatic fetch integration remain open at https://github.com/home-lang/home/issues/873. Node and global resource state are not yet unified.",
    "Further argument/coercion, selective clearing, native base-class interactions, full resource semantics and platform coverage remain open under #869 and #66.",
    "The valid manual Node API control and selected passing scope do not prove complete global/fetch resource timing.",
    "Pickier reports no errors and four existing style warnings.",
    "Windows measurement, Linux execution, wider startup paths, prior ICU contradiction #872, complete Bun suite, remaining native/API ownership and Release/ASAN/all-platform verification remain open under #66."
  ],
